        "text": "Char\nThe [char] type describes a single character, a member of the UTF-16 character set that we\u2019re currently\nusing. It\u2019s a 16-bit value that corresponds to a symbol in the current character map. Try the following:\n[char]$MyChar = 24\n$MyChar\nOn my machine, I see an up-arrow \u2191 . You may see something different. What you won\u2019t see is 24 .\nWe did something new there; we preceded the variable with a type accelerator. To understand why,\nwe need to talk about typing.",
